refined_lab_test:
One Kaggle CPU lab run on all 199 videos with OOF DaughterNet p. Base: exp48 (+ef if probe 29 holds).
Configs: cap 4 (control), cap 5, cap 6 and cap 8 at the shipped threshold, plus cap 4 at threshold minus 0.1.
Log per config and per embryo:
- divins_added and divins_skipped_cap_frame;
- evaluable dTP/dFP vs the previous cap step;
- the edge-term delta, separately;
- the score delta and the division-J sign under J_s = 0.13 / 0.20 / 0.25 / 0.36.
Decision rule, fixed before the run: adopt a higher cap only if all of these hold:
- cumulative marginal evaluable precision beyond cap 4 is >= 0.25 with >= 8 marginal evaluable forks;
- the pooled score delta vs cap 4 is >= +0.0005;
- no embryo is negative.
Otherwise close the item. The prior evidence (0/2 at cap 4 -> 6) says it will close. Cost: one CPU kernel run, no GPU.
